  "deviations_from_standard": [
    "Port counts: the TSW202 has 8 copper and 2 SFP ports, so the standard's ranges map to port1-4 AP trunk, port5 IoT access, port6-7 Internal access, port8 copper uplink trunk, sfp1-2 SFP uplink trunk.",
    "BPDU guard: not supported on the TSW202. Access ports use STP edge plus loop detection instead.",
    "Storm control 5%: not supported. The lowest TSW202 preset is 240 Mbit/s, which is below the 1 Gbit/s link rate, so storm control is left disabled.",
    "Access-port frame filtering: the TSW202 has no admit-only-untagged setting. Access ports are members of a single untagged VLAN only.",
    "NTP: the operator specified 129.6.15.28 and 129.6.15.29. The standard names dh1 (100.126.15.28).",
    "RADIUS login authentication (100.126.15.28:1812): not configured. It needs a RADIUS secret, which is a separate credential step.",
    "Management restriction: the TSW202 has no source-address ACL. Management is reachable only through the VLAN 10 interface address. IPv6 link-local remains on the management VLAN.",
    "SNMP: the standard's read-only community for LibreNMS is set per device in NetBox and is not available on the 192.168.10.0/24 island. The factory communities are removed. Firmware 10.2 requires the SNMP agent while LLDP is on, so the agent runs with v1/v2c off, v3 only and no users, which answers no request."
